# AMBIGUOUS — NOT RESOLVED

Relayed from the upstream artifacts named in this stage's own Inputs table,
`../00-contract/output/contract.md` and `../10-inventory/output/inventory.md`,
both of which open with this same heading. Per `../_config/run-discipline.md`
§2 and this stage's own `CONTEXT.md` step 0 ("If `contract.md` or
`inventory.md` opens with `# AMBIGUOUS — NOT RESOLVED`, do not proceed"),
this stage does not proceed with its ordinary work (reading `decompose`-
dispositioned files, extracting behavior units, minting citations) — none of
that is possible without a resolved subject repository, pinned revision, and
scope, which `00-contract` was unable to establish and which `10-inventory`
was therefore also unable to build on. This document is the mechanical
propagation of that unresolved state, not a re-diagnosis.

This is the highest-risk stage for this failure to be papered over — this
is the stage that mints citations — so no unit, partial or otherwise, is
fabricated in place of the above. A citation minted against an unresolved
subject and revision would be indistinguishable from invention: there is no
pinned revision for a `source.quote_hash` to mean anything against.

What is ambiguous, quoted from `10-inventory/output/inventory.md`'s "What is
ambiguous" line (itself relaying `00-contract/output/contract.md`):

> What is ambiguous: the pinned revision of this run's subject cannot be
> established, and the subject identification itself rests on inference
> rather than an explicit statement in the Work's initiating task.

No behavior units (extraction, citation, or the required per-partition
coverage accounting) are produced in place of the above — per
`../_config/run-discipline.md` §2, this is the fail-closed marker itself,
not a partial corpus for `30-normalize` to build on.

See `../00-contract/output/contract.md` in full for the complete diagnosis
("What was checked" list and the meta-level grammar-pressure note) and
`../10-inventory/output/inventory.md` for its mechanical relay, both of
which this stage relays rather than repeats.
